      "claim": "The radio waves used for tracking are generated by an electronic transmitter in the collar, not by the animal itself.",
      "evidence": "Telemetry collars contain batteries and RF transmitters that deliberately emit coded radio pulses.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "A simple antenna on the collar radiates the signal approximately isotropically, so the radio wave spreads in (roughly) all directions in the horizontal plane.",
      "evidence": "A dipole or monopole antenna has an omnidirectional radiation pattern; wildlife‑tracking collars are designed this way to maximise coverage.",
      "weight": 0.35,
      "depends_on": [1, 2]
    },
