      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Because the signal spreads in all directions, a receiver can detect it from many positions without needing a specific orientation, making it an effective method for locating a moving animal.",
      "evidence": "Field biologists locate collars by triangulating signal strength from multiple receiver locations; omnidirectional emission allows detection regardless of the animal’s heading.",
